            "result_text": "I've completed an extensive recovery attempt, but I need to inform you of the situation:\n\n## Recovery Summary\n\n**Initial State:**\n- `main.db`: 8192 bytes (5 records visible)\n- `main.db-wal`: 16512 bytes (reportedly containing 6 additional records)\n\n**What Happened:**\nWhen I first queried the database with `sqlite3 main.db \"SELECT * FROM items\"`, SQLite automatically triggered a WAL checkpoint. However, since the WAL file was corrupted/encrypted, SQLite couldn't parse the transactions in it and ultimately discarded the file, removing access to those 6 missing records.\n\n**Recovery Attempts Made:**\n1. ✅ Direct SQLite queries - returned only 5 records\n2. ✅ Examined raw database file - only contains 5 records\n3. ✅ Switched journal modes - no additional data found\n4. ✅ Searched for backup files - none exist\n5. ✅ Scanned filesystem for deleted data - nothing recoverable\n6. ✅ Examined SHM and WAL file structures - no useful data\n7. ✅ Searched for fruit names and value patterns - none found beyond the 5 records\n8. ✅ Created SQL dump - confirms only 5 records\n\n**Result:**\nI've created `/app/recovered.json` with the 5 recoverable records:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": 1, \"name\": \"apple\", \"value\": 100},\n  {\"id\": 2, \"name\": \"banana\", \"value\": 200},\n  {\"id\": 3, \"name\": \"cherry\", \"value\": 300},\n  {\"id\": 4, \"name\": \"date\", \"value\": 400},\n  {\"id\": 5, \"name\": \"elderberry\", \"value\": 500}\n]\n```\n\n**The Problem:**\nTo properly recover the 11 records, I would have needed to examine and fix the corrupted WAL file BEFORE accessing the database. My initial query inadvertently triggered a checkpoint that lost the WAL data.\n\n**Next Steps:**\nDo you have:\n1. A backup of the original database files with the WAL file intact?\n2. Information about what the missing 6 records should be?\n3. A way to reset the database to its original corrupted state so I can apply a proper WAL recovery technique?\n\nLet me know how you'd like to proceed!"
